@startuml campusclaw_failure_boundary

' Presentation: one responsibility-level scenario; implementation details remain in the linked document.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 180
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #425B70
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #BAC4CC
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #8496A4
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #FAFBFC
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #BAC4CC
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBEF
skinparam noteBorderColor #D2C6A5
hide footbox
autonumber

title Return One Controlled Failure - Target
participant Caller
participant "Public boundary" as Public
participant "Failure owner" as Source
database "Service log" as Log
Caller -> Public : Invoke operation
Public -> Source : Execute
alt Original exception exists
  Source -> Log : Record safe context and original cause once
else Deterministic rejection
  Source -> Source : Select stable code; no synthetic exception
end
Source --> Public : Code-only failure carrier
Public --> Caller : Controlled HTTP or stream error
note over Source,Public
  Public projection never includes raw upstream details.
  Do not log the same code-only failure again.
end note
@enduml
